ngspice-rs — NOTICE

This repository is a from-scratch Rust implementation ("the port") of ngspice,
the SPICE circuit simulator.

Upstream project:   ngspice
  https://ngspice.sourceforge.io/
  git://git.code.sf.net/p/ngspice/ngspice
Reference revision:  pre-master-48 @ 059066b53

The port is a derivative work of ngspice: it reimplements behaviour that
ngspice's C sources define, and the doc comments throughout `src/` name the
upstream file and function each piece has to match. Paths such as
`src/spicelib/parser/inpeval.c` and `src/frontend/rawfile.c` are paths **in the
upstream ngspice tree**; they are not paths in this repository, which does not
vendor the C sources.

ngspice is distributed under a Modified BSD license. The license text, and the
list of contributions that carry different terms, is in COPYING; attribution is
in AUTHORS. Both files are reproduced here verbatim from upstream. Where the
port translates rather than reimplements, the upstream terms are the ones that
apply: `src/maths/sparse` (SPARSE 1.3) carries the permissive Berkeley notice
below, and `src/maths/KLU` is LGPLv2. Nothing is taken from KLU.

`src/maths/sparse13.rs` is a Rust translation of SPARSE 1.3, Kenneth S.
Kundert's sparse matrix package (advising professor Alberto
Sangiovanni-Vincentelli, UC Berkeley), as distributed in ngspice's
